      "id": "71cef6d273d3-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "In which year was the foundation stone for the Gateway of India laid in Bombay (now Mumbai)? &#2348;&#2377;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2375; (&#2309;&#2348; &#2350;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2312;) &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2327;&#2375;&#2335;&#2357;&#2375; &#2321;&#2347; &#2311;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2358;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2352;&#2326;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2341;&#2368;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In which year was the foundation stone for the Gateway of India laid in Bombay (now Mumbai)?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2348;&#2377;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2375; (&#2309;&#2348; &#2350;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2312;) &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2327;&#2375;&#2335;&#2357;&#2375; &#2321;&#2347; &#2311;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2358;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2352;&#2326;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2341;&#2368;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "1920 1920",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1920</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1920</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "1915 1915",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1915</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1915</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "1911 1911",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1911</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1911</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "1905 1905",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1905</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1905</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>The Gateway of India is an arch monument built during the 20th century in Bombay, India. The monument was erected to commemorate the landing of King George V and Queen Mary at Apollo Bunder on their visit to India in 1911.</p><p>Built in Indo-Saracenic style, the foundation stone for the Gateway of India was laid on <u>31 March 1911</u>. The structure is an arch made of basalt, 26 metres (85 feet) high. The final design of George Wittet was sanctioned in 1914 and the construction of the monument was completed in 1924. The Gateway was later used as a symbolic ceremonial entrance to India for Viceroys and the new Governors of Bombay. It served to allow entry and access to India.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "71cef6d273d3-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "The Howrah bridge was officially opened in the year _______. &#2361;&#2366;&#2357;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332; &#2310;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2340;&#2380;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; _______ &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The Howrah bridge was officially opened in the year _______.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2361;&#2366;&#2357;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332; &#2310;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2340;&#2380;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; _______ &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404;</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "1943 1943",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1943</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1943</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "1948 1948",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1948</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1948</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "1930 1930",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1930</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1930</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "1935 1935",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1935</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1935</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>&bull; The <b>Howrah Bridge</b>, also known as the <b>Rabindra Setu</b>, was officially opened to the public in <b>1943</b>.</p><p>&bull; It is located in <b>Kolkata (formerly Calcutta)</b>, India, and connects the city to the Howrah district.</p><p>&bull; The bridge is a <b>suspension bridge</b> and is one of the busiest in the world, serving as a critical transportation link.</p><p><b>Details:</b></p><p>&bull; Construction began in <b>1936</b>, and after seven years of building, it was officially inaugurated in <b>1943</b>.</p><p>&bull; It was built without any nuts and bolts, using riveting instead.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
